+# rev0846 change summary
+
+## Main risk addressed
+
+rev0846 closes two remaining symlink-boundary gaps on the future publication path. rev0845 rejected symlinked rights targets and public-surface payload reads, but a local rights file could still be reached through a symlinked intermediate directory, and queue/decision metadata could still be loaded through symlinked JSON files before publication output creation.
+
+## Code changes
+
+- `scripts/publication_rights_gate.py` now uses `_first_symlink_component()` for local rights targets. The fresh scan rejects `docs/link/LICENSE` when `docs/link` is a symlink, even when it resolves back inside the archive.
+- `scripts/publish_queue_item.py` now uses `first_symlink_component()` / `fail_on_symlink_path()` for queue metadata reads, decision metadata reads, `CHANGELOG.md`, SHA-256 inputs, and archive file path validation.
+- Queue-state and decision JSON iteration are now explicit helper functions, so symlinked queue directories or JSON files fail closed before target bytes are read.
+
+## Audit and validation additions
+
+- `scripts/validate_publication_rights_gate_intermediate_symlink_rev0846.py`
+- `scripts/validate_publish_queue_item_metadata_symlink_rev0846.py`
+- `AUDIT/PUBLICATION_RIGHTS_GATE_INTERMEDIATE_SYMLINK_REV0846.md` / `.json`
+- `AUDIT/PUBLISH_QUEUE_ITEM_METADATA_SYMLINK_REV0846.md` / `.json`
+- `VALIDATION/rev0846_targeted_validation.txt`
+
+## Refreshed carried-forward surface
+
+- `AUDIT/PUBLICATION_PREFLIGHT_DRY_RUN_SAFETY_REV0840.md` / `.json`
+
+## Deliberately unchanged
+
+- The rev0840 canonical patch streams remain unchanged so previous patch-application validation remains interpretable.
+- No root `LICENSE`, `COPYING`, final `NOTICE`, component license conclusion, or SPDX/RO-Crate rights assertion was invented.
+- Canonical-tree surfaces remain carried as canonical-tree surfaces rather than silently reinterpreted as rev0846 release surfaces.
+
+## Rights status
+
+Still publication-blocked. This revision makes future publication metadata handling harder to trick through symlinks; it does not resolve owner/upstream rights decisions.
+
+---
